{
  "title": "FHL Tendonitis & Injuries",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7024/fhl-tendonitis-and-injuries",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 25 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "FHL Tendonitis & Injuries occur as a result of impingement of the flexor hallucis longus tendon with resultant tendonitis and even tendon rupture along the posterior ankle joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with posteromedial ankle pain and pain with resisted flexion of the hallux IP joint. MRI studies may show tenosynovitis of the tendon.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally rest, activity modifications and NSAIDs. Surgical management is indicated for acute FHL tendon laceration and progressive tendonitis that fails nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior ankle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "great toe",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "excessive plantar-flexion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dancers in on pointe position",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "gymnasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "activities involving maximal plantar-flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterior to the talus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "within the fibro-osseous tunnel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "in chronic cases nodule formation may lead to triggering",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior ankle impingement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "os trigonum (posterolateral tubercle)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Muscle",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "FHL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "originates from posterior fibula",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "travels between posteromedial/posterolateral tubercles of the talus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "contained within fibro-osseous tunnel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "passes beneath the sustentaculum tali",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "crosses dorsal to FDL (at the Knot of Henry)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "FHL is \"higher\" at Knot of Henry",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "FDL is \"down\" at Knot of Henry",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "multiple connections exist between the FDL and FHL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "distally it stays dorsal to the FDL and neurovascular bundle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inserts on the distal phalanx of the great toe",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Biomechanics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "primary action",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "plantarflexion of the hallux IP and MP joints",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "secondary action",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "plantarflexion of the ankle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posteromedial ankle pain**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "great toe locking with active range of motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "crepitus along the posterior medial ankle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dancers will typically endure symptoms for a longer period of time prior to seeking orthopaedic care when compared to non-dancers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain with resisted flexion of the IP joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain with forced plantarflexion of the ankle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**great toe triggering** with active or passive motion but no tenderness at the level of the first metatarsal head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
